U ls
C List  information  about  the FILEs.
U cd
C Can change of folders.
U cat
C Concatenate FILE(s) to standard output.
U pwd
C Print the full filename of the current working directory.
U mkdir
C Make directories.
U rm
C Remove files or directories.
U cp
C Copy files and directories.
U mv
C Move (rename) files.
U touch
C Update the access and modification times of each FILE to the current time.
U man
C An interface to the system reference manuals.
U grep
C Print lines that match patterns.
U find
C Search for files in a directory hierarchy.
U chmod
C Change file mode bits (change permissions).
U chown
C Change file owner and group.
U sudo
C Execute a command as another user.
U df
C Report file system disk space usage.
U du
C Estimate file space usage.
U top
C Display Linux processes.
U ps
C Report a snapshot of the current processes.
U kill
C Send a signal to a process.
U tar
C An archiving utility.
U ssh
C OpenSSH SSH client (remote login program).
U scp
C Secure copy (remote file copy program).
U curl
C Transfer a URL.
U wget
C The non-interactive network downloader.
U head
C Output the first part of files.
U tail
C Output the last part of files.
U ln
C Make links between files.
U echo
C Display a line of text.
